From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niranjan H Y <niranjan.hy@ti.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:25:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: intel_auxdevice: add tac5xx2 family to
 wake_capable_list

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167689

Add tac5572, tac5682 to the wake_capable_list as it can generate jack
events whilst the bus is stopped.

Signed-off-by: Niranjan H Y <niranjan.hy@ti.com>
Signed-off-by: Bard Liao <yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260901012812.231057-1-yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 1d4d3198ccce18ec1d58ac41c47e7b2aabba2e94)
Signed-off-by: Chris Chiu <chris.chiu@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00341
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@fb051c37e27ce2dd68bc3dbd1e93cba5c679c718
---
 drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c b/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
index a8407560bf4f..f5124621c52f 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
@@ -74,6 +74,8 @@ static struct wake_capable_part wake_capable_list[] = {
 	{0x025d, 0x721},
 	{0x025d, 0x722},
 	{0x04b3, 0x9356},
+	{0x0102, 0x5572},
+	{0x0102, 0x5682},
 };
 
 static bool is_wake_capable(struct sdw_slave *slave)
